    "note": "2026-10-24 dependency review preparation for hbrowser 0.45.2 with dev-only distlib>=0.4.4: fresh official build/dev metadata confirms build 1.6.1, distlib 0.4.4, hatchling 1.32.4, mypy 2.4.0, packaging 26.3, pytest 9.1.1 and ruff 0.17.2 remain within all declarations. Distlib 0.4.4 release-note research covers launcher/shebang and archive-filtering corrections; its 3.14 classifier and universal wheel support the development-tool requirement, with Windows behavior still requiring platform validation. Fresh official PyPI metadata confirms unchanged stable versions asyncio-atexit 1.0.1, beautifulsoup4 4.15.0, h2h-galleryinfo-parser 0.5.3, httpx 0.28.1, websockets 17.3 and zendriver 0.17.1. All satisfy current runtime declarations, admit Python 3.14 through Requires-Python and provide compatible wheels. No newer stable release lies outside current bounds; retain the documented exact Zendriver lifecycle cohort. Reused the hash-verified 2026-10-22 official release-note/README/sdist research because both versions and constraints are unchanged. Metadata/wheel compatibility is not behavioral acceptance; canonical hbrowser lifecycle/navigation/challenge/timeout/process-tree and parser tests remain separate evidence. Public release notes remain unavailable for h2h-galleryinfo-parser; asyncio-atexit has upstream README but no changelog in the previously inspected official sdist. Fresh npm metadata confirms markdownlint-cli2 0.24.0 satisfies >=0.18.1 and Node >=22; current Node 24.22.1 qualifies. Preserve current bounds and exact zendriver==0.17.1; no new runtime incompatibility was identified. Unchanged versions reuse the explicitly attributed hash-verified prior note research, not newly claimed note reads; no tests or installs were performed for this preparation.",
